<h3>Guild Roles<o:p></o:p></h3>

<p><b>Raid Commander</b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p>The sole responsibility of the Raid Commander is to arrange and organize a
guild-wide raid. This can be anything from a basic raid of Cazic Thule to a Planes
raid. The Raid Commander should discuss the raid planning with an officer of
the Circle of Bones and set the goals for the raid (are we going after a
specific critter? Are we &quot;doing&quot; a dungeon? Are we there to learn the
zone? etc.). Once the raid place, date, time, and goals have been established
and approved by the Circle of Bones, the raid will be announced on the guild
website at least 5 days in advance and announced on guild chat.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p>The Raid Commander is expected to be at the raids planned. If the Raid
Commander cannot be there for some reason (real life obligations, etc.). The
Raid Commander must appoint a temporary &quot;Raid Master&quot; who will be in
charge of conducting the raid and must be present at the raid<o:p></o:p></p>

<p><b>Recruiters</b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p>The recruiting position is an important role within the guild. They are the
main contact between the guild and new potential members. All inquiries about
guild membership should be directed to one of the guild recruiters. The
responsibilities of a recruiter includes:<o:p></o:p></p>

<ol start=1 type=1>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'>Be the initial contact with
     new potential members and a public relations to help recruit new members. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'>Make sure that potential
     member fit within the Bloodhorde guidelines. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'>Get a good feeling for
     potential new members and filter out the &quot;not so good&quot; ones. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l2 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list .5in'>Send a weekly email report to
     the Circle of Bones listing any new recruits. <o:p></o:p></li>
</ol>

<p><b>Guild Meeting Coordinator</b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p>Responsible for organizing one guild-wide meeting (in guild chat) and one
Circle of Bones meeting a month.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p><b>Guild Recruit Initiator</b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p>Reponsible for properly initiating all new members by setting up duels for
them and providing an initiation ceremony.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p>&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>

<p><b>Battalion Dragoon and Crusader</b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p>The Battalion Dragoon and Crusader are to be considered co-leaders of a
battalion. The Dragoon and Crusader are to be the same level range as their
battalion and are expected to hunt with their battalion. The Dragoon and
Crusader are responsible for choosing the hunting spot for their Battalion. The
hunting spot should have a priority of good experience for members of the
Battalion, with possible item drops as a distant secondary concern, unless
otherwise directed by their commanding Blood Knight. The Battalion is strongly
encouraged to stay at a chosen hunting spot for at least one week. This allows
members of the battalion to get there, get bound near by, and have a consistent
place to hunt with guild members without the need to run around the world each
time they log on. <o:p></o:p></p>

<p>The Dragoon and Crusader are given different roles and responsibilities for
clarity. However, either one should should be able to handle all
responsibilities if the other is not present.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p>Since the Dragoon and Crusader are required to hunt with their battalion.
There will come a time when they have advanced in level beyond their own
battalion. At this point the Dragoon and Crusader should consult with each
other and pick a member from their battalion that is worthy of taking over the
position. Once they have chosen a person to fill the vacant position, they
should discuss it with their commanding Bone Guard or Blood Knight. If it is
approved, the chosen member will be moved to the Dragoon or Crusader position.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p><b>NOTE</b>: It should be made clear that if a member is a Dragoon or
Crusader of a lower level Battalion, it does not guarantee that they will hold
that position in a higher level battalion. Do not expect to be promoted to
Dragoon/Crusader again just because you were a Dragoon/Crusader before. When
you move up, there are many people in front of you for that position.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p><b>Battalion Dragoon</b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p>Overall, the Dragoon is responsible for the management of the Battalion. The
Dragoon responsibilities include:<o:p></o:p></p>

<ol start=1 type=1>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list .5in'>Be the leader and morale
     boost for their Battalion <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list .5in'>handle all Battalion issues
     (member conflicts, arguments, etc.). If the Dragoon is unable to resolve
     an issue, he/she should contact their commanding Bone Guard. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list .5in'>Posting the current hunting
     spot on the Battalion's page on the website. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list .5in'>Loot distribution - the
     Dragoon is responsible for making sure their Battalion understands how
     items are distributed and enforcing/encouraging that distribution method.
     It is strongly suggested that the guild <a href="..\rules\Loot.htm">Loot
     Distribution</a> rules and guidelines are followed. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l1 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list .5in'>Finding new hunting spots <o:p></o:p></li>
</ol>

<p><b>Battalion Crusader</b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p>The Crusader focuses on the hunt and battle. The Crusader responsibilities
include:<o:p></o:p></p>

<ol start=1 type=1>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:list .5in'>Be the leader and morale
     boost for their Battalion <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:list .5in'>Strongly encourage members to
     hunt at the chosen hunting spot. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:list .5in'>Actively work to make sure
     their battalion members are grouped with each other as much as possible.
     This also includes telling who to group with who and rearranging groups as
     necessary to make the hunt as productive and fun as possible. <o:p></o:p></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:auto;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo3;tab-stops:list .5in'>Help members work on battle
     strategies <o:p></o:p></li>
</ol>

<p class=MsoNormal><![if !supportEmptyParas]>&nbsp;<![endif]><o:p></o:p></p>

